# The deployment URL from `npx convex dashboard` / `npx convex dev`'s output.
VITE_CONVEX_URL=https://giddy-retriever-468.convex.cloud

# That is the only variable this SPA needs. Sign-in moved to Convex Auth
# (convex/auth.ts), so the OAuth exchange happens on the Convex deployment
# and the client id/secret live there, not in the browser bundle:
#
#   npx convex env set AUTH_GOOGLE_ID     <client id>.apps.googleusercontent.com
#   npx convex env set AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET <client secret>
#   npx convex env set SITE_URL           https://canvas.iota.uz
#   node scripts/setup-auth-keys.mjs      # generates + sets JWT_PRIVATE_KEY, JWKS
#
# (`npx @convex-dev/auth` also generates those keys, but it is the interactive
# scaffolder: it rewrites tsconfig.json and offers to overwrite convex/auth.ts,
# auth.config.ts and http.ts, all of which are hand-written here.)
#
# The OAuth client also needs this redirect URI registered in Google Cloud
# Console: https://giddy-retriever-468.convex.site/api/auth/callback/google

# Written by scripts/dev-agent.mjs into .env.local (not here) when you run the
# isolated local stack: the shared secret /dev/sign-in signs in with. Unset
# everywhere else, which is what keeps that page inert.
# VITE_DEV_AUTH_SECRET=
